@rafaelfranca I still get the deprecation warning on 82ab90365330e22614c73a5900f12dbc6e9c352b :
"DEPRECATION WARNING: Initialization autoloaded the constants ActionText::ContentHelper and ActionText::TagHelper."
So #40222 doesn't fix this.

> Maybe a stupid question but how did you all figure out where the issue was in your apps? I'm about to start digging through my app and the Gemfile but would be nice to have some direction before I start 😁

@jacobwalkr A pretty simple, if inelegant, brute-force solution did the trick for me.  Once I figured out that another gem is the culprit, I started commenting out various non-essential/less-popular gems (and any associated initializers) and run `rails c`.  Once I got the console to run without the deprecation message, I started un-commenting out the gems one-by-one, until I found the one causing problems.  

Having said that, if you have good test coverage, I would start with updating as many gems as you are comfortable with.
